  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1250 PM CDT Tue Sep 29 2026\n\nTuesday night - Monday\n\nAn Upper-lvl ridge will continue to migrate over the region, \nallowing dry conditions and low 90s high temps to stick around for \nanother day. A \"Limited\" fire danger will continue over northern \nparts of the area as RH values (%) remain in the mid-20s. Continue \nto heed any local burn bans and be cautious of outdoor burning. \nWinds will gradually shift to the south, increasing moisture and RH \nvalues Thursday into the weekend.  \n\nAn upper-lvl low from the Southwest region and the absorbed remnants \nof Hurricane Polo will push a frontal boundary towards the region. \nRain chances will return as the frontal boundary approaches Friday, \nlasting through the weekend. Although hazardous weather is not \nexpected, forecast trends will be monitored as the week progress. 50-\n85% probability for rain are expected with the high probabilities on \nSaturday (70-90%) and Sunday (60-75% areawide). WPC estimates \nrainfall totals of 2-4 inches over the weekend, which would help \nimprove ongoing drought conditions. /SW/",
